Spec: SpecDD Syntax Highlighting

Platform: IntelliJ Platform / Kotlin

Purpose:
  Provide syntax highlighting for SpecDD `.sdd` files.

Structure:
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighter.kt: IntelliJ syntax highlighter and lexer tokenization boundary.
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighterFactory.kt: IntelliJ syntax highlighter factory.
  ./SpecDDHighlightingColors.kt: Highlighting attribute keys and default attributes.
  ./SpecDDColorSettingsPage.kt: IntelliJ color scheme integration for SpecDD highlighting keys.
  /src/main/resources/colorSchemes/SpecDDDefault.xml: Default editor color attributes for bundled light schemes.
  /src/main/resources/colorSchemes/SpecDDDarcula.xml: Default editor color attributes for bundled dark schemes.

Owns:
  ./highlighting.sdd
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighter.sdd
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighterFactory.sdd
  ./SpecDDHighlightingColors.sdd
  ./SpecDDColorSettingsPage.sdd
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighter.kt
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighterFactory.kt
  ./SpecDDHighlightingColors.kt
  ./SpecDDColorSettingsPage.kt

Can modify:
  ./highlighting.sdd
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighter.sdd
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighterFactory.sdd
  ./SpecDDHighlightingColors.sdd
  ./SpecDDColorSettingsPage.sdd
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighter.kt
  ./SpecDDSyntaxHighlighterFactory.kt
  ./SpecDDHighlightingColors.kt
  ./SpecDDColorSettingsPage.kt

Can read:
  /src/main/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/parser/*
  /src/test/kotlin/ai/specdd/idea/highlighting/*

Must:
  Highlight SpecDD syntax without validating document correctness.
  Depend only on shared language contracts when cross-package support is needed.
  Use `@SpecDDLineClassifier` as the shared line-classification boundary.
  Register an IntelliJ `@SyntaxHighlighterFactory` that returns `@SpecDDSyntaxHighlighter`.
  Register an IntelliJ `@ColorSettingsPage` so SpecDD semantic highlighting keys are exposed in standard editor color schemes.
  Provide bundled color-scheme defaults through IntelliJ `additionalTextAttributes`.
  Use non-deprecated highlighting key registration APIs.
  Keep highlighting behavior covered by Kotest BehaviorSpec tests.
  Keep syntax highlighter behavior, color keys, color scheme integration, and factory behavior in separate file-level contracts.

Must not:
  Report validation diagnostics.
  Add plugin-specific settings or configuration UI.
  Decide whether a section name, task state, indentation, or structure is valid.
  Add inspections, annotations, quick fixes, or error reporting.
  Define validation severity or inspection messages.
